        You chuckle, asking if that isn’t what he wanted. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I didn’t think it would be that fast! Can you stop me?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Noah</span> calls out as he swings back and forth, no longer using his legs as he tucks them in out of fear. <span style="color:Pink">The way his voice changes volume as he swings towards you than away is rather cute. You push him once more, causing the boy to begin giggling out of fear, before you eventually slow him down.</span> <br>
        <br>
        Once the swing is still, he quickly jumps off of it and collapses into the sand. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Haha, maybe- maybe that was a LITTLE too high.”</span> <span style="color:Pink">He says between deep breaths, his cheeks flushed from laughter, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Felt like I was going to fall off… can we do it again!?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Noah</span> jumps to his feet, almost stumbling back to the ground from how quick it was, before leaping back onto the swinging and giving you a hopeful smile. Seems he may have become a bit of an adrenaline junky.</span> <br>
        <<addMoodlet "Stress" 0>>
